# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Built binaries. The stock template only covers extensions, which catches
# nothing on Linux — `go build ./cmd/skyl-gateway` produces a 22 MB file named
# exactly this, and `git add -A` would happily commit it.
/gateway/skyl-gateway
/skyl-gateway
/skyl-sandbox

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
#
# go.work is deliberately NOT ignored. The stock Go template ignores it because
# a workspace usually points at directories outside the repository, which are
# personal to whoever made it. Ours points only at this repository's own three
# modules, so it is the shared development setup — it replaces the `replace`
# directives that used to live in each go.mod, and CONTRIBUTING.md tells people
# to use it. Ignoring it would mean every contributor recreating it by hand.
#
# go.work.sum stays ignored: it is derived, and each module's own go.sum is the
# checksum record that actually ships.
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
